WEBVTT

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:11.210
What happens when you type a URL into your
browser?

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:14.810
Think of the internet like a massive phone
system.

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:18.350
Your browser knows the name you typed,
like example.com,

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.170
but it needs a phone number, called an IP
address,

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:22.890
to actually call the server.

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:26.270
It asks a DNS server, which acts like an
address book,

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:27.990
to swap that name for a number.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:32.270
Once the browser has the address, it
reaches out to the server.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.250
They start with a TCP handshake, which is
just a way of saying

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.830
"Are you there?" and "Yes, I'm ready."
Only then does the browser send a GET…
